          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
          gameplay: "1. First Betting: After the initial cards are dealt, the player with the highest card starts the betting.\n2. The Reveal: The dealer turns cards from the undealt deck one at a time.\n3. Matching: If the turned card matches a player's rank, that player takes the card.\n4. Betting Rounds: Every time a match occurs, a new round of betting begins, led by the player with the most cards (or highest rank if tied).\n5. Discards: If a card doesn't match anyone's held rank, it is discarded, and the next card is flipped.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Four of a Kind.',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Two-pot system: High pot (four-of-a-kind or best hand) and Low pot (lowest 5-card hand).',
            'Winning condition: Collect all four cards of your starting rank OR hold the lowest total hand when someone else completes their set.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "If your starting rank is high (Aces or Kings), you can be more aggressive in early betting. If your rank is low, you should 'check' and 'call' to stay in the game for the Lowndpot half.",
          intermediate: 'The Fold Decision: If two cards of your rank are discarded early (because they were dealt as initial cards to others or flipped before you), you cannot win the Highndpot. You must then pivot to having the lowest total hand or fold to minimize losses.',
          advanced: "Pot Odds: Calculate how many 'live' cards are left for your rank versus your opponents. If you have 3 cards and there is only 1 left in the deck, but your opponent has 1 and 3 left, your odds of hitting Four-of-a-Kind are significantly higher.",
          tips: [
            "Stay in if you have a low rank (2s or 3s) even if you aren't getting matches; you are the favorite for the Lowndhalf of the pot.",
            "Fold early if you have a midndrange card (7s or 8s) and you aren't getting matches, as you are unlikely to win either the High or the Low pot.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
